 "comment": "tds_payees, #1243: TDS on vouchers that share a GUID. Contractor H: four bills of Rs 29,000 cross the aggregate; two blank-GUID journals each carry Rs 1,000 of TDS against it: Rs 2,000 of TDS is seen, on two vouchers. Contractor J: three blank-GUID plain bills of Rs 50,000, each carrying its own TDS: July's at the higher rate (deducted on its own voucher, listed on the TDS question), August's two short of the lower rate and between the rates, in a month the challans show nothing deposited for (clause 21(b)(ii)(B)). Contractor S: two blank-GUID bills of Rs 28,000, each also crediting Helper T and carrying Rs 500 of TDS the books do not divide: each bill with that TDS is Rs 28,500, under the single sum, and the two under the aggregate.",
